WEBVTT

00:06.047 --> 00:08.049
[theme music playing]

01:03.313 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:06.066 --> 01:07.817
[breath trembling]

01:09.819 --> 01:10.653
[gasps]

01:11.738 --> 01:13.281
What the actual fuck?

01:13.823 --> 01:15.116
[gasps]

01:16.951 --> 01:20.330
Please spare me. Please.

01:20.413 --> 01:22.373
With those hands
that pushed a person,

01:23.166 --> 01:24.542
you're begging for your life?

01:25.418 --> 01:27.629
-Your damn hands…
-[panting]

01:27.712 --> 01:28.671
…know no shame.

01:33.718 --> 01:35.678
[Jun-u screams]

01:35.762 --> 01:37.347
[rumbling in distance]

01:40.683 --> 01:44.604
We've confirmed his existence,
but you're now a widow, Mom.

01:45.814 --> 01:47.190
It was about time.

01:47.816 --> 01:53.071
The question is, did he save Ki Ka-young
on his own, or did she wish to be saved?

01:53.154 --> 01:54.489
That level of rage

01:55.323 --> 01:56.866
suggests she didn't wish it.

01:56.950 --> 01:59.035
[wind blowing]

02:07.252 --> 02:08.920
[men groan]

02:11.756 --> 02:12.715
[Wahid] Father!

02:14.968 --> 02:16.803
[in Arabic] You, human,
have lived 1000 years

02:16.886 --> 02:18.930
and are still none the wiser!

02:20.473 --> 02:24.269
You should be grateful
that she didn't make her final wish.

02:24.352 --> 02:26.813
[in Arabic]
If that were her final wish,

02:27.313 --> 02:29.315
I could search for the unclaimed lamp

02:29.399 --> 02:31.359
and take it for my own.

02:31.442 --> 02:33.319
You are no spirit. What are you?

02:33.403 --> 02:37.574
[Ejllael] All of that girl's wishes
were for the sake of others.

02:37.657 --> 02:41.327
Her final wish must also be
a righteous one.

02:42.245 --> 02:43.454
Should my plan work,

02:43.955 --> 02:46.708
the only future Iblis faces
is annihilation.

02:47.667 --> 02:51.588
This means that he will never
be able to serve another master.

02:52.505 --> 02:55.008
So even if the owner of the lamp dies,

02:55.508 --> 02:57.385
I cannot take it for myself?

02:57.468 --> 02:59.971
You mere half-spirit.

03:00.722 --> 03:04.183
Do not dare to stir my wrath
or meddle any further in my affairs.

03:04.267 --> 03:07.937
I am Ejllael, the angel of death,
and I will be Iblis's undoing.

03:08.521 --> 03:12.442
This is your final warning.

03:24.954 --> 03:27.206
-[Wahid in Korean] Father!
-[man] Are you okay, Father?

03:37.175 --> 03:38.801
Is my boss okay?

03:39.469 --> 03:41.095
She took some meds and dozed off.

03:42.096 --> 03:43.264
Sade.

03:43.848 --> 03:45.183
I have somewhere to visit.

03:45.767 --> 03:47.477
Protect the clay lump while I'm away.

03:48.728 --> 03:52.440
If the need arises, I'm saying
you may use your mystical powers.

03:53.858 --> 03:54.692
Yes, Master.

03:57.445 --> 04:00.448
[somber music playing]

04:44.826 --> 04:47.829
[Iblis speaking in Arabic]
It's been a long time, Brother.

04:48.871 --> 04:51.457
I haven't seen you
since the days of the war.

04:55.795 --> 04:57.588
It seems your garden

04:58.214 --> 05:00.091
has changed quite a bit,

05:00.967 --> 05:01.926
hasn't it?

05:02.010 --> 05:05.346
[In Arabic] Brother, have you forgotten
how you once spoiled my flowers?

05:06.472 --> 05:12.103
And do you not remember
how I stood at the front line of the war

05:12.186 --> 05:13.354
while you sat back?

05:13.438 --> 05:15.898
Come on, why are you even here?

05:19.068 --> 05:21.195
Do you grow any foreign species?

05:21.779 --> 05:26.200
[scoffs] If the wind carries
foreign seeds this way,

05:26.284 --> 05:27.285
I tend to them.

05:28.536 --> 05:29.370
Why do you ask?

05:31.372 --> 05:34.709
Then did a foreign seed with shaggy hair

05:34.792 --> 05:38.212
fly this way from the East in 1041?

05:40.298 --> 05:45.011
And when did the flower
of this seed wither away?

05:45.094 --> 05:51.100
Ah. So you are here
to fill a void in your memory.

05:53.561 --> 05:55.813
What do you think happened, Iblis?

05:55.897 --> 05:57.899
[soft suspenseful music playing]

06:09.243 --> 06:11.162
[coughing]

06:12.455 --> 06:14.332
-[Shadi] Khalid!
-[coughing]

06:16.793 --> 06:19.629
[in Arabic] It seems your cough has
worsened. Are you okay, Khalid?

06:21.672 --> 06:24.092
[in Arabic] You don't
get sick or die, Father.

06:24.175 --> 06:28.971
All I am capable of doing
is weaving these unbreakable threads.

06:29.055 --> 06:32.350
[coughs] Why am I such a weak being?

06:33.434 --> 06:35.853
Why did you make me
such an imperfect being?

06:37.563 --> 06:40.191
Humans grow sick and eventually die,

06:41.317 --> 06:45.071
but that is exactly what makes them
shine so brightly while they live.

06:45.154 --> 06:48.032
I don't want to hear it!
You are a complete spiritual being,

06:48.116 --> 06:53.996
yet all you can do for your dying son
is offer him a mere apple.

07:00.920 --> 07:02.380
[man speaking Arabic] Hey, you!

07:02.964 --> 07:05.258
Catch him! He stole my bread!

07:05.341 --> 07:06.968
Catch the boy!

07:09.554 --> 07:11.139
-[grunts]
-[man] You little rat!

07:11.222 --> 07:12.557
How dare you steal from me!

07:12.640 --> 07:14.267
You little rascal!

07:14.350 --> 07:17.603
I'll show you.
I'll teach you a lesson you won't forget!

07:17.687 --> 07:18.729
[Shadi] Stop that.

07:21.190 --> 07:23.526
He is just a hungry little boy.

07:24.944 --> 07:27.864
Unless you're going to pay,
you should stay out of it.

07:37.832 --> 07:40.042
[In Mongolian] Here, we can share this.

07:42.879 --> 07:44.046
Wait, boy.

07:44.547 --> 07:47.383
I see you have an immortal body.

07:49.719 --> 07:51.387
[In Mongolian] That is not my fault.

07:58.436 --> 08:01.397
[Iblis speaking in Arabic]
So Shadi changed their souls.

08:16.537 --> 08:19.457
Shadi must have put his sick son's soul

08:20.958 --> 08:22.543
into an immortal body.

08:22.627 --> 08:23.711
Yes, he did.

08:25.421 --> 08:27.340
And I helped him.

08:30.927 --> 08:33.596
For doing so, I was punished.

08:35.515 --> 08:40.144
Since that day,
no soul's seeds have blessed my garden.

08:40.645 --> 08:44.190
But that foreigner's flower
is still in bloom,

08:44.273 --> 08:46.192
very much alive, as you can see.

08:58.037 --> 09:02.875
MAN FOUND DEAD AFTER TRAIL COLLAPSE
ON MOUNT CHEONGPUNG

09:05.294 --> 09:08.172
-[elevator dings]
-[footsteps approaching]

09:11.175 --> 09:12.927
[man speaking in Korean]
Who are you people?

09:13.010 --> 09:15.805
Why are you lurking outside my home? Huh?

09:16.347 --> 09:17.265
Dad?

09:17.932 --> 09:19.183
I missed you!

09:19.267 --> 09:21.310
I found my way home! I'm a good boy!

09:21.394 --> 09:24.730
You fucking scared me, you creep.
You must be barking mad.

09:24.814 --> 09:27.358
Yes, I am barking. It's me, Ppoppi.

09:27.441 --> 09:29.902
[panting excitedly] I'm so sorry.

09:29.986 --> 09:31.445
I lost you, Dad.

09:32.029 --> 09:33.197
What?

09:36.117 --> 09:38.160
Ha-neul! My dear baby brother, Ha-neul!

09:39.120 --> 09:40.746
Who are you, punk?

09:40.830 --> 09:43.874
How do you know my son's name? [yelps]

09:44.542 --> 09:46.127
Hands off my boss, sir.

09:46.210 --> 09:47.628
[Kim Gae] Ha-neul.

09:47.712 --> 09:49.213
It's your big brother.

09:49.297 --> 09:51.799
Dad. It's me, Ppoppi.

09:55.219 --> 09:56.262
That's right.

09:56.345 --> 09:58.180
-Chauffeur Kim.
-[man winces]

09:58.264 --> 09:59.974
I need to make another wish.

10:00.766 --> 10:03.019
Let's go to Cheongpung Village.

10:03.519 --> 10:04.353
Quick.

10:05.271 --> 10:06.105
Ppoppi, bang!

10:07.732 --> 10:08.649
[panting]

10:09.984 --> 10:10.818
Ppoppi, "v."

10:12.903 --> 10:14.238
-Ppoppi, nose.
-Hey.

10:14.322 --> 10:16.407
[panting]

10:16.490 --> 10:20.328
Ppoppi, I missed you.

10:20.411 --> 10:22.455
-Daddy. It's Ppoppi.
-[man] Yeah?

10:23.039 --> 10:25.374
But, Ppoppi, how did you become human?

10:25.958 --> 10:28.544
I wished for it.

10:29.045 --> 10:30.963
I've wanted to tell you something.

10:32.506 --> 10:35.926
-[whispering]
-You lunatic, get away from him!

10:37.053 --> 10:39.347
You crazy bastard… [groans]

10:42.767 --> 10:46.354
Ha-neul. Just wait a short while, okay?

10:47.605 --> 10:50.858
You wait too, Dad. Okay?
"That's it. Good boy."

10:51.442 --> 10:53.986
-He's insane.
-Chauffeur Kim, start the engine.

10:54.570 --> 10:56.489
-Start the engine.
-Hurry back!

11:01.952 --> 11:03.245
ODD TEETH AND ODD PEOPLE WELCOME

11:03.329 --> 11:04.580
[Mi-ju] Wisdom teeth?

11:04.664 --> 11:06.957
[Min-ji] Your gums are swollen,
so we can't extract today.

11:08.918 --> 11:10.836
We'll take X-rays to check for impaction.

11:10.920 --> 11:13.881
Yes, ma'am.
I'll let you gargle before we move on.

11:13.964 --> 11:17.468
Goodness. I'm pushing 80
and growing wisdom teeth?

11:19.011 --> 11:21.347
Will this take long?
I'm due at the food bank.

11:22.473 --> 11:23.307
Mm.

11:25.851 --> 11:26.852
[gargles]

11:33.776 --> 11:37.446
Wow, for such a young lady,
you sure are good in the kitchen.

11:37.988 --> 11:39.990
I only ever knew
to cook for my own family.

11:40.074 --> 11:43.869
-I'm just happy that I can help.
-[woman chuckles]

11:43.953 --> 11:45.704
Why, hello!

11:45.788 --> 11:47.373
-Hello.
-[all] Hello.

11:48.541 --> 11:51.377
He funds the food bank. CEO Ryu Su-hyeon.

11:51.460 --> 11:54.839
This is our newest volunteer,
Ms. Lee Mi-ju.

11:55.881 --> 11:57.007
I'm happy to see you.

11:58.717 --> 12:00.302
I was hoping we'd meet.

12:00.928 --> 12:03.431
[Mi-ju] What the…
Why would he hope to meet me?

12:03.931 --> 12:06.475
Don't tell me… [gasps]

12:06.559 --> 12:10.146
Oh Pan-geum, you little minx!

12:11.313 --> 12:13.816
Why would you be happy to see me?
We've never met.

12:14.400 --> 12:17.111
[chuckles] I don't think that's true.

12:18.070 --> 12:20.948
Humans really do cherish youth,
don't they?

12:22.658 --> 12:26.495
It's not like a youthful exterior
adds years to your lifespan.

12:27.246 --> 12:28.247
How foolish.

12:28.330 --> 12:30.833
[ominous music playing]

12:30.916 --> 12:32.543
Lifespan?

12:34.670 --> 12:35.796
Wait there!

12:37.840 --> 12:39.425
Excuse me, Mr. Ryu!

12:39.508 --> 12:41.969
Why did you just say that to me?

12:45.931 --> 12:48.684
Why did I say that?
Do you really want to know?

12:48.767 --> 12:52.271
You've met a spirit and now an angel.
You are quite the lucky one.

12:53.689 --> 12:55.107
What do you mean by…

12:56.066 --> 12:57.485
An angel?

12:59.487 --> 13:00.905
[gasping]

13:03.407 --> 13:06.035
I am the angel Ejllael,

13:06.660 --> 13:08.370
also known as the angel of death.

13:09.914 --> 13:11.916
Of death?

13:11.999 --> 13:13.959
You foolish, arrogant human.

13:14.627 --> 13:17.713
Did you think volunteering
would lighten the burden of your secret?

13:18.380 --> 13:21.550
With your regained youth, did you dream
of living a long, happy life?

13:21.634 --> 13:23.177
That dream is but a delusion.

13:24.345 --> 13:25.554
What in the world

13:26.388 --> 13:27.348
do you mean?

13:27.431 --> 13:30.559
You may have gained youth,
but your remaining time is unchanged.

13:30.643 --> 13:34.813
Though you will go to heaven since
you lovingly took in your granddaughter.

13:34.897 --> 13:36.565
You may find solace in that.

13:44.156 --> 13:45.366
When the plum blossoms

13:46.575 --> 13:49.036
next bloom in your garden…

13:50.829 --> 13:52.039
you will die.

13:52.122 --> 13:54.124
[ominous music playing]

14:02.466 --> 14:04.802
We can't apologize enough.

14:05.469 --> 14:08.556
The entire sum that was transferred
due to a processing error

14:08.639 --> 14:11.183
has been returned
to your account, Ms. Ki Ka-young.

14:14.937 --> 14:15.813
Okay.

14:16.855 --> 14:20.985
I'm a little unwell as I fell off a cliff
recently, so I'll take my leave now.

14:23.946 --> 14:24.947
-Right.
-[manager] Right?

14:25.030 --> 14:27.199
What seems to be the…

14:27.283 --> 14:28.909
Perhaps the amount is incorrect?

14:28.993 --> 14:30.202
No, it's correct.

14:31.954 --> 14:32.997
I'll take this money

14:33.664 --> 14:35.082
entirely in cash.

14:36.125 --> 14:39.503
[spluttering] The entire amount in cash?

14:40.045 --> 14:45.092
Uh… But with such large amounts,
you need to disclose the intended use.

14:45.593 --> 14:47.887
It is
an especially large amount, after all.

14:48.679 --> 14:52.933
People usually just say
it's going toward their wedding fund--

14:53.017 --> 14:56.186
Sure, then it's marriage funds for me too.

14:57.396 --> 14:59.690
The entire amount. In cash.

15:00.733 --> 15:02.443
You psycho bitch!

15:02.985 --> 15:04.486
Ms. Gu Bo-gyeong!

15:15.915 --> 15:17.791
[Ka-young] These jerks. [scoffs]

15:20.920 --> 15:21.754
Hmm.

15:27.885 --> 15:30.888
[vehicles approaching]

15:33.933 --> 15:37.353
[tense music playing]

15:37.436 --> 15:39.438
[car doors open]

15:40.940 --> 15:43.484
[car doors close]

15:51.575 --> 15:53.410
I heard about your hiking accident.

15:53.911 --> 15:55.829
As a friend, I thought I'd check in.

15:56.413 --> 15:57.331
Friend?

15:58.082 --> 16:01.585
That would complicate things since
your dad and I went to college together.

16:02.252 --> 16:04.463
Or does it not matter now that he's dead?

16:05.381 --> 16:07.007
So I guess you know it all now.

16:07.591 --> 16:08.467
Who I am.

16:10.803 --> 16:12.221
I have an inkling.

16:13.722 --> 16:14.723
Is it you?

16:15.391 --> 16:17.476
The first wish I made in my past life?

16:18.686 --> 16:19.603
So not everything.

16:21.230 --> 16:26.151
[man speaking in Arabic] It's Shaytan!
It's the wrath of Iblis!

16:26.235 --> 16:28.112
Khalid! Khalid!

16:30.698 --> 16:31.824
Khalid!

16:35.828 --> 16:37.162
What on earth have you done?

16:38.539 --> 16:42.543
You're half right, half wrong. You started
this, so you should end it too.

16:43.877 --> 16:45.170
Where is the lamp?

16:45.254 --> 16:47.047
I hear you have one wish left.

16:47.798 --> 16:49.258
Would you use it for my sake?

16:50.342 --> 16:53.679
I'd really like to put an end
to this tiresome immortality.

17:03.022 --> 17:04.398
I've caught you red-handed.

17:04.481 --> 17:05.566
Pure bullshit.

17:05.649 --> 17:08.193
[tense music playing]

17:10.279 --> 17:11.739
I trust you've got my back.

17:20.664 --> 17:22.833
[growling]

17:22.916 --> 17:24.251
[man yelps]

17:27.796 --> 17:28.922
[growling]

17:32.426 --> 17:34.053
[Ka-young] It heals right away.

17:34.762 --> 17:36.555
Not even a slit throat could kill you.

17:36.638 --> 17:37.890
Unfortunately.

17:38.390 --> 17:41.351
[Chang-sik] We've got you now, we have!

17:41.435 --> 17:43.729
-What are you-- Hey!
-[yelps]

17:43.812 --> 17:45.105
It's a jaguar. A jaguar.

17:45.189 --> 17:49.151
He and I go back to the 11th century.
They're the ones making threats.

17:49.234 --> 17:52.154
Yes, we know. We've seen them before too.

17:53.238 --> 17:55.449
[in English] Hey, do you remember me?

17:56.158 --> 17:59.161
[in Korean] Now decide. Will you get
caught alive? Or caught as ghosts?

17:59.244 --> 18:00.704
Either way, you will be caught.

18:00.788 --> 18:03.082
You know, all of us Korean mens

18:03.165 --> 18:06.210
have a military obligation,
so we're almost killers. Of those, we…

18:06.293 --> 18:07.377
Let us retreat.

18:16.345 --> 18:17.888
[Chang-sik chuckles] See that?

18:17.971 --> 18:21.391
They're all scaredy-pants.
I could just… They're all scaredy-pants.

18:22.392 --> 18:23.227
Are you okay?

18:23.727 --> 18:25.979
They seemed off,
so we've kept an eye on them,

18:26.063 --> 18:28.190
and those jerks have been tailing you.

18:28.273 --> 18:31.568
What's stranger is that every day,
another one of them disappears.

18:31.652 --> 18:34.822
Someone dies in that house
every single day!

18:34.905 --> 18:37.324
[cars departing]

18:37.407 --> 18:38.742
-Mr. Park.
-Yeah?

18:38.826 --> 18:40.494
-I have a favor to ask.
-Yeah?

18:40.577 --> 18:42.246
This may sound strange,

18:42.329 --> 18:45.374
but you have all just entered
a very strange world.

18:46.208 --> 18:48.127
-Like the existence of this jaguar.
-[growls]

18:48.210 --> 18:49.294
Yikes.

18:52.172 --> 18:53.298
I'll be fine,

18:53.382 --> 18:56.718
so please watch Mi-ju,
the lady at my house, and Min-ji.

18:56.802 --> 18:59.596
So what you're saying is that those two

18:59.680 --> 19:03.559
can't know what's going on,
but they also can't get caught off guard?

19:03.642 --> 19:04.476
That's right.

19:04.560 --> 19:05.644
Don't you worry.

19:05.727 --> 19:06.562
Yes.

19:07.146 --> 19:10.357
Seeing this guy in person,
I can see he's actually quite tame.

19:10.440 --> 19:12.568
-Like a pet jaguar.
-[low growling]

19:12.651 --> 19:14.778
-[snarls]
-I'm glad we could clear the air.

19:14.862 --> 19:17.281
Get him! I'm scared. Get him!

19:20.450 --> 19:22.077
[wind blowing]

19:30.502 --> 19:32.921
[Shadi] Long time no see, Brother.

19:33.005 --> 19:36.008
-You have come to see me at my worst.
-[in Arabic] It seems so.

19:36.592 --> 19:39.428
It's been a long time, my brother.

19:41.138 --> 19:42.639
[Shadi] Should I be worried?

19:43.182 --> 19:45.601
Does your being here
mean my son is in danger?

19:48.061 --> 19:48.896
Perhaps.

19:50.147 --> 19:51.398
How I have resented

19:51.481 --> 19:53.275
the wish of your master

19:54.651 --> 19:57.487
and your reckless decision
to create an immortal body.

19:57.571 --> 19:58.405
Khalid!

19:58.488 --> 20:01.617
How I regret putting
my son's soul into that body.

20:03.577 --> 20:04.411
Yes.

20:05.245 --> 20:08.040
I was, indeed, arrogant.

20:08.707 --> 20:12.044
That's why I have come.
To give you a chance.

20:12.127 --> 20:17.674
Your son will never claim
her final wish as his own.

20:18.634 --> 20:21.845
To be human is to make one's own choice.

20:22.346 --> 20:24.014
However he may threaten her,

20:24.097 --> 20:28.227
her final wish will
most certainly be righteous.

20:28.810 --> 20:32.272
So you believe in your master?
That faith will cost you your life.

20:33.649 --> 20:35.025
So be it.

20:35.609 --> 20:38.987
I have already decided
to go to hell, Shadi.

20:40.364 --> 20:43.450
So if you wish to protect your son,

20:43.951 --> 20:46.411
do not let things get that far.

20:47.037 --> 20:50.207
If your son insists
on making the wrong decision

20:50.958 --> 20:52.459
and becomes my master,

20:53.543 --> 20:54.920
I will kill him.

21:00.676 --> 21:04.638
[sighs] I cannot stop my son for too long.

21:04.721 --> 21:07.683
That would mean
the death of innocent children.

21:09.851 --> 21:12.354
So, he is even more evil than I.

21:13.522 --> 21:15.649
A true shaytan.

21:15.732 --> 21:19.569
I will try to hold him back
for as long as I can.

21:20.779 --> 21:23.365
That is the best I can do.

21:25.158 --> 21:27.119
If that is your best, my brother,

21:27.202 --> 21:31.415
I am afraid you must worry
for your son's fate.

21:32.249 --> 21:37.963
I refuse to show your son any more mercy.

21:38.046 --> 21:40.048
[tense music playing]

21:54.062 --> 21:56.523
CLOSED TEMPORARILY
DUE TO PERSONAL REASONS

21:57.816 --> 21:59.359
[in Korean] Right, that's her there.

21:59.443 --> 22:00.694
-Oh, it's her?
-[chuckles]

22:00.777 --> 22:03.488
Earlier today, I saw her
leave the bank with bags of cash.

22:04.406 --> 22:06.116
But they say she's a psycho.

22:06.199 --> 22:09.411
Is that right?
Then it makes sense for her to be rich!

22:09.494 --> 22:11.621
-I'm a fan of Professor Park Ji-seon.
-[dialing]

22:11.705 --> 22:15.292
She says psychopaths are more likely
to be successful than normal folk like us…

22:15.792 --> 22:16.960
This fucking bitch!

22:19.004 --> 22:21.089
[tense music playing]

22:23.675 --> 22:27.596
Oh, shh. Why get smacked
when we could just talk things out?

22:27.679 --> 22:30.223
Hey, Miss Psycho.
Why don't we share that cash?

22:30.807 --> 22:34.603
[intermittent rumbling]

22:37.355 --> 22:39.357
[tense music continues playing]

22:49.826 --> 22:52.120
Wait, that guy…

22:52.746 --> 22:55.207
Were those stairs always there?

22:55.832 --> 22:58.293
I'm sure they weren't there a minute ago.

23:03.340 --> 23:06.510
I left Sade with you.
Was my showing up really necessary?

23:07.719 --> 23:09.638
He went outside to relieve himself.

23:10.138 --> 23:12.682
By the way,
I was just smacked really hard.

23:12.766 --> 23:14.309
Get your ass over here!

23:15.268 --> 23:16.394
You were smacked?

23:16.895 --> 23:17.896
Wow.

23:18.688 --> 23:20.982
Now that's something I won't tolerate.

23:21.775 --> 23:24.361
-[men grunt, yelp]
-[rock fusion music playing]

23:26.655 --> 23:28.115
-What is that?
-What was that?

23:28.698 --> 23:31.076
[all screaming]

23:31.660 --> 23:34.079
[grunts, sighs]

23:34.913 --> 23:36.998
[screaming]

23:39.751 --> 23:40.710
Be right back.

23:48.260 --> 23:50.762
Hey, why are you tagging along?

23:54.391 --> 23:55.684
[sighs] Huh?

23:56.643 --> 23:59.062
[yelping] Please save me!

23:59.146 --> 24:01.898
I swear I'll live an honest life
from now on!

24:01.982 --> 24:03.942
[screaming] What is this place?

24:05.485 --> 24:06.778
Where are we?

24:09.030 --> 24:10.282
What is all this?

24:11.283 --> 24:12.117
Where are we?

24:12.200 --> 24:15.078
The place I fell to
when I was booted from heaven.

24:16.163 --> 24:17.080
Hell.

24:19.082 --> 24:20.208
You were here?

24:21.710 --> 24:22.711
For how long?

24:24.504 --> 24:25.505
I'm not sure.

24:26.339 --> 24:27.549
For a time

24:28.049 --> 24:31.928
that you guys call "eternity." [chuckles]

24:33.096 --> 24:36.433
This is how far you'd go
to avoid bowing to humans?

24:37.767 --> 24:38.602
Even now?

24:40.562 --> 24:41.813
That would be the case.

24:43.899 --> 24:47.444
Just to be sure,
you'll take me out of here, won't you?

24:47.527 --> 24:49.446
Others barely consider me human, you know.

24:51.114 --> 24:55.243
I just want to be sure too.
About the 1,000 won you never gave me.

24:55.327 --> 24:58.038
And about dinner,
the thing you frequently didn't give me.

24:58.121 --> 24:59.581
And about the straw cutter.

24:59.664 --> 25:02.667
That time you didn't fetch
the hand straw cutter, but the huge--

25:03.710 --> 25:07.297
I'm treating you with care.
My dear Genie is warm-- [grunts]

25:07.881 --> 25:09.549
Whoa, hold up there.

25:10.383 --> 25:14.179
-And I am refusing. [giggles]
-Mm. Hmm.

25:15.430 --> 25:17.265
I guess this is just… [grunts]

25:19.184 --> 25:21.186
…how it is between us. Come here.

25:23.772 --> 25:24.773
Get over here.

25:29.527 --> 25:31.404
[footsteps approaching]

25:31.488 --> 25:33.490
Why are you so late?
I told you to fly over!

25:33.573 --> 25:37.869
Where would I get a velvet hanger
at this hour? I was lucky Irem had one.

25:37.953 --> 25:39.579
What do you even need this for?

25:39.663 --> 25:42.666
From now on,
you and I need to work together.

25:44.251 --> 25:45.085
Now.

25:45.669 --> 25:48.129
Pull it very carefully from top to bottom.

25:48.630 --> 25:51.091
We can't let a single speck of dust
fall off this.

25:51.174 --> 25:54.552
Hell's dust, air, vibe,
saturation, and brightness.

25:54.636 --> 25:57.430
Every molecule and atom,
memory, and recollection.

25:57.514 --> 25:59.182
Dust from hell?

26:02.686 --> 26:06.022
You seem upbeat,
considering you just took a trip to hell.

26:06.106 --> 26:09.818
I avoided every one of her shots today.
She didn't land a single one.

26:10.318 --> 26:14.656
I guess I've just worked out your pattern.
Right, left, left, center. [scoffs]

26:14.739 --> 26:15.782
[in English] Easy.

26:15.865 --> 26:17.158
[Ka-young in Korean] Not likely.

26:18.201 --> 26:19.202
Hang it up over there.

26:20.787 --> 26:21.621
[Sade] Okay.

26:22.747 --> 26:25.792
The immortal being was that kid.
My upperclassman's son.

26:26.918 --> 26:28.795
He came to see me at the auto shop.

26:30.171 --> 26:32.340
You're half right and half wrong.

26:34.050 --> 26:35.552
He said that too.

26:35.635 --> 26:37.595
Why am I only ever half right?

26:37.679 --> 26:39.264
What is right, and what is wrong?

26:40.307 --> 26:43.268
Shadi switched the souls of his son
and the immortal being.

26:44.477 --> 26:48.231
The boy you hoped would live a long life
never got to do so.

26:49.774 --> 26:51.109
The immortal being…

26:53.111 --> 26:53.945
is Khalid.

26:55.238 --> 26:56.573
Khalid.

26:57.449 --> 26:58.950
The one I saw in the hourglass?

26:59.993 --> 27:03.371
That brat. I was nice to him,
and this is how he treats me?

27:04.331 --> 27:06.499
[Gae] Mr. Genie!

27:08.168 --> 27:09.002
Mr. Genie!

27:10.503 --> 27:11.921
I found my dad.

27:12.005 --> 27:15.884
I was so excited to see
my baby brother Ha-neul again! [sniffing]

27:15.967 --> 27:17.135
Are you

27:17.635 --> 27:18.470
Kim Gae?

27:19.721 --> 27:23.224
Oh. You really do look like Daniel Henney.

27:23.725 --> 27:25.852
[snarling]

27:25.935 --> 27:27.228
-Down boy.
-[barks]

27:28.146 --> 27:29.564
Oh. [in English] Sorry.

27:30.690 --> 27:32.692
[in Korean] Force of habit. [laughs]

27:32.776 --> 27:33.985
Mr. Genie.

27:34.069 --> 27:37.530
Please turn me back into a dog.

27:37.614 --> 27:38.448
[in English] Please.

27:41.826 --> 27:43.828
[gags]

27:43.912 --> 27:44.871
[in Korean] Boss!

27:45.663 --> 27:46.790
What's wrong?

27:47.290 --> 27:48.583
Are you ill in some way?

27:49.167 --> 27:52.879
-Let's get you to a hospital now.
-No. No. [coughs]

27:53.505 --> 27:56.925
Every time I go to the hospital,
I feel sleepy.

27:57.008 --> 27:58.802
"How will we pay for the surgery?"

27:59.302 --> 28:00.553
Dad gets angry.

28:00.637 --> 28:02.138
Ppoppi.

28:02.222 --> 28:05.308
[in English] Bad boy.
Bad boy. [coughs]

28:05.392 --> 28:07.519
[Chauffeur Kim]
Let me at least wipe the blood.

28:08.478 --> 28:11.981
Why do you keep seeing yourself as a dog?

28:12.065 --> 28:15.485
In my life, I've met a lot of people
who were absolute dogs.

28:17.320 --> 28:19.406
But you're a really good man.

28:19.489 --> 28:20.740
Chauffeur Kim.

28:21.366 --> 28:23.910
Thank you so much for everything.

28:24.494 --> 28:28.081
You can have all of my money.
I don't need it anymore.

28:29.457 --> 28:31.376
Mr. Genie, please hurry.

28:31.960 --> 28:33.253
That's truly your final wish?

28:34.838 --> 28:36.756
Why not go ask while you're still human?

28:36.840 --> 28:39.843
If they've lost a dog,
if they're looking for one, if they even…

28:42.053 --> 28:42.887
want to find it.

28:43.471 --> 28:44.305
None of that

28:45.181 --> 28:46.141
matters anymore.

28:47.183 --> 28:50.270
I need to say goodbye
to Ha-neul as Ppoppi.

28:50.353 --> 28:51.396
Boss.

28:51.479 --> 28:53.064
So I have to go.

28:54.023 --> 28:56.818
This… is my final wish.

28:56.901 --> 28:59.738
[melancholic music playing]

28:59.821 --> 29:01.322
[sighs] This is so screwed up.

29:15.587 --> 29:16.880
It's been fulfilled.

29:22.427 --> 29:24.429
[panting]

29:32.437 --> 29:35.106
[poignant music playing]

29:38.985 --> 29:40.153
[whines]

29:48.661 --> 29:49.871
[mouse clicks]

29:56.795 --> 29:58.797
-[mouse clicks]
-[officer] She got to the terminal,

29:58.880 --> 30:01.966
didn't get on a bus,
but went out and got into a taxi?

30:03.885 --> 30:04.928
Why is that?

30:07.472 --> 30:08.890
[Ka-young] If that kid is Khalid,

30:08.973 --> 30:11.976
then can't you just go to that time
and see what happened?

30:12.560 --> 30:13.937
I've already tried.

30:14.521 --> 30:16.981
But I can't go
to that specific period of time.

30:17.065 --> 30:18.107
Why not?

30:18.191 --> 30:19.984
I think he's hiding it from me.

30:20.485 --> 30:23.988
He had also been granting me three wishes.

30:25.114 --> 30:26.699
Your connections are just, wow.

30:28.201 --> 30:29.994
So? What did you wish for?

30:30.078 --> 30:31.830
My first wish

30:32.372 --> 30:35.375
was to be able to send humans to hell
with three wishes.

30:36.417 --> 30:37.335
The second

30:37.418 --> 30:41.464
was to release me from the lamp
so I may meet and corrupt a new master.

30:42.507 --> 30:44.050
So you have one wish left?

30:46.177 --> 30:47.512
That's what I thought too.

30:50.515 --> 30:51.558
But…

30:53.935 --> 30:56.145
I think I've already made

30:57.564 --> 30:59.190
all three of my wishes.

31:03.194 --> 31:04.696
[in Arabic] I have another question.

31:05.280 --> 31:08.616
Back in 1041,

31:08.700 --> 31:12.704
another foreign seed would
have flown this way.

31:13.872 --> 31:14.956
You're right.

31:18.877 --> 31:21.588
It was a rather striking flower
from the East.

31:22.422 --> 31:26.801
At first, it was wilted
and on the verge of dying.

31:27.719 --> 31:31.973
But it sprang back to life
and bloomed for 28 years before fading.

31:34.642 --> 31:36.895
Not eight years?

31:36.978 --> 31:38.021
No.

31:39.022 --> 31:40.982
It bloomed for another 20 years.

31:43.526 --> 31:46.988
That flower was in full bloom
in the wasteland of your memory.

31:52.452 --> 31:54.704
[in Korean] I'm not sure
what I wished for…

31:55.288 --> 31:58.249
[screaming]

31:58.333 --> 31:59.500
…but I think…

32:03.087 --> 32:04.756
it led to a very grim end.

32:11.179 --> 32:12.430
So I'm scared.

32:17.060 --> 32:19.062
I know how it feels to be scared now.

32:20.229 --> 32:23.524
When I was falling off the cliff,
I thought of Grandma, Min-ji…

32:25.777 --> 32:26.778
and you.

32:27.737 --> 32:29.906
The thought of never
seeing any of you again

32:31.491 --> 32:34.285
seriously pissed me off.
That's being scared, isn't it?

32:36.663 --> 32:37.664
You're not far off.

32:39.499 --> 32:44.003
So I've climbed pretty high up the ranks.
I beat out the auto shop and even frogs.

32:44.545 --> 32:47.507
[sighs] It was really tough
with the frogs.

32:47.590 --> 32:48.591
[chuckles]

32:52.762 --> 32:55.640
It seems like you also need
one of those places right now.

32:57.642 --> 32:59.852
A place like rooftops are to me.

33:01.145 --> 33:01.980
Got one?

33:08.236 --> 33:09.529
This is last spring.

33:11.572 --> 33:13.241
This is that kind of place for you?

33:14.784 --> 33:19.122
Is this when the bats, snakes,
cockroaches, and the like come out?

33:19.998 --> 33:21.666
[Iblis] Stop that. I get squeamish.

33:21.749 --> 33:23.751
Sea louse, woodlouse.

33:23.835 --> 33:25.628
I said stop it.

33:26.212 --> 33:28.297
Do you think that fits
the reason we're here?

33:29.298 --> 33:30.758
[Ka-young] That's too bad.

33:30.842 --> 33:32.844
I know a ton of disgusting things.

33:34.679 --> 33:36.222
Why do you like it here anyway?

33:36.806 --> 33:37.890
Uh…

33:39.225 --> 33:40.560
It was just so pretty.

33:42.979 --> 33:44.897
I'd lived such a long life,

33:46.399 --> 33:47.734
never seeing cherry blossoms.

33:51.696 --> 33:54.157
At the time, I remember wanting
to see them with you.

33:54.240 --> 33:55.324
At the time?

33:56.826 --> 33:58.578
But that time was during the festival.

33:59.078 --> 34:01.873
Wasn't that the time
when you were trying your hardest

34:02.790 --> 34:03.624
to kill me?

34:05.001 --> 34:06.544
[romantic ballad playing]

34:06.627 --> 34:09.380
I stopped trying my hardest.

34:10.381 --> 34:11.340
From that moment on.

34:15.386 --> 34:17.305
If I had tried my hardest,

34:17.805 --> 34:19.223
you'd be dead.

34:35.031 --> 34:36.616
So it was from that moment on.

34:37.950 --> 34:39.494
When the flowers withered,

34:41.079 --> 34:42.997
you grew uneasy
at the thought of me dying.

34:53.216 --> 34:55.426
And here I was, thinking I was first.

35:08.147 --> 35:09.190
How pretty.

35:09.690 --> 35:11.692
[ballad continues playing]

35:29.293 --> 35:30.336
[ballad ends]

35:31.462 --> 35:34.382
Is that true?
The immortal one visited Ki Ka-young?

35:35.716 --> 35:38.344
YES. HE WENT PERSONALLY
TO THE AUTO SHOP

35:40.721 --> 35:41.931
That bumbling idiot!

35:42.807 --> 35:45.977
[groans] I overestimated
the patience of humans.

35:47.895 --> 35:48.813
Wait, no.

35:48.896 --> 35:51.315
At the rate he's going,
I should be using him.

35:52.108 --> 35:53.693
Is the lamp the only way?

35:55.486 --> 35:58.114
COULD YOU PLEASE REPEAT THAT FOR ME?

35:58.197 --> 35:59.574
I COULDN'T READ YOUR LIPS

35:59.657 --> 36:02.451
Come on. [sighs]

36:05.788 --> 36:07.456
-Have you thought about what you did?
-Mm.

36:07.540 --> 36:09.792
-Will you do it again?
-Mm.

36:10.835 --> 36:12.170
[sighs]

36:24.807 --> 36:28.311
When the plum blossoms
next bloom in your garden,

36:28.895 --> 36:30.229
you will die.

36:32.690 --> 36:33.774
[exhales sharply]

36:39.405 --> 36:41.032
Why isn't she coming?

36:41.532 --> 36:42.909
-Ms. Yoo?
-Yes?

36:43.409 --> 36:46.913
Could you send me Lee Mi-ju…
I mean, Ms. Ki Ka-young's X-rays?

36:46.996 --> 36:47.830
Sure.

36:49.123 --> 36:52.710
By the way, why are you treating her
under Ms. Ki Ka-young's name?

36:53.586 --> 36:55.338
Because I own this dental clinic.

36:56.214 --> 36:57.048
Right.

36:57.632 --> 36:58.925
The file is with you now.

37:02.220 --> 37:03.512
KI KA-YOUNG

37:04.764 --> 37:05.598
Huh?

37:08.976 --> 37:11.062
OH PAN-GEUM

37:15.524 --> 37:17.401
KI KA-YOUNG
OH PAN-GEUM

37:19.987 --> 37:22.531
OH PAN-GEUM

37:24.784 --> 37:27.620
KI KA-YOUNG
OH PAN-GEUM

37:33.251 --> 37:37.213
[Pan-geum] Buy ten kilos of sun-dried
salt. I'm going to mix the soybean paste.

37:47.807 --> 37:49.267
What are you doing here?

37:49.350 --> 37:50.977
Oh. It's you, Ka-young.

37:52.061 --> 37:53.729
You see that vest?

37:57.817 --> 37:58.693
Vest?

37:58.776 --> 38:02.363
Ka-young. I can't tell anyone else,

38:02.446 --> 38:04.824
but you've always been a little strange.

38:05.324 --> 38:07.493
The thing is…

38:07.576 --> 38:09.328
My daughter-in-law…

38:09.412 --> 38:11.580
Well, ex-daughter-in-law
since they're divorced.

38:11.664 --> 38:17.003
I hear she drinks her days away, hung up
on being fired after 20 years as manager.

38:18.254 --> 38:21.841
But I can't shake the image
of her always worn out,

38:22.758 --> 38:24.969
thinking a bottle of face cream
was a luxury,

38:25.052 --> 38:26.887
standing there in that vest.

38:30.516 --> 38:31.350
Mother!

38:32.059 --> 38:33.060
Mother!

38:33.144 --> 38:34.729
"Mother"!

38:35.604 --> 38:37.481
I could swear she once called out to me.

38:38.441 --> 38:41.485
[inhales sharply]
I have no clue what this is.

38:42.069 --> 38:43.779
Maybe I'm getting dementia.

38:47.783 --> 38:49.785
[Ka-young] You spirits or angels
or whatever.

38:50.453 --> 38:52.621
You all pretend to be so mighty,

38:52.705 --> 38:54.123
but just look at Granny An.

38:54.623 --> 38:55.458
She's still

38:55.541 --> 38:59.920
holding on to a fragment of the memories
you erased with your magic.

39:03.174 --> 39:05.092
That doesn't change a thing.

39:05.926 --> 39:07.511
It only adds to the suffering.

39:10.014 --> 39:10.848
Well…

39:12.850 --> 39:14.518
I guess we'll just suffer, then.

39:22.735 --> 39:26.155
By the way,
why did you scribble all over your lamp?

39:26.238 --> 39:27.448
Were you badmouthing me?

39:28.240 --> 39:30.409
Scribble? In the lamp?

39:32.286 --> 39:33.579
I did nothing of the sort.

39:37.291 --> 39:40.044
What are you saying is here? Where?

39:41.295 --> 39:42.505
What do you mean?

39:43.005 --> 39:47.885
There are a whole lot of Arabic letters
all over the walls and floor here!

39:48.719 --> 39:51.222
-Huh?
-You really can't see this?

39:51.972 --> 39:53.015
Never mind. Move.

39:57.895 --> 39:59.897
[intriguing music playing]

40:28.509 --> 40:31.512
So you're saying this is written
here in my lamp?

40:33.931 --> 40:35.307
See? It's there, right?

40:35.808 --> 40:38.144
If you can read it, go ahead.
What does it say?

40:41.272 --> 40:44.400
"You, who came from Goryeo,
were living as a slave."

40:44.900 --> 40:46.444
"Serves you right."

40:46.527 --> 40:48.154
-See? It's there…
-[music stops]

40:48.988 --> 40:51.740
So you were badmouthing me.
Trying to die, are we?

40:51.824 --> 40:53.242
[beckons]

40:54.160 --> 40:55.828
Here. What does this say?

40:59.248 --> 41:04.295
"Who in their right mind would sell
date palms if they don't make any money?"

41:05.296 --> 41:08.174
What a load of shi… sheer brilliance.

41:08.257 --> 41:11.177
Go on. Keep reading.
I'll deal with you later.

41:20.853 --> 41:24.773
"Even though I told you I'm a genie,
you keep wishing on stars…"

41:28.569 --> 41:32.072
"No matter how much I tell you,
you wish on silly stars."

41:32.698 --> 41:35.868
"But you keep wishing for me to do well."

41:37.119 --> 41:40.456
"You must really think
I'm a poor peddler."

41:41.081 --> 41:43.083
[gentle music playing]

41:45.377 --> 41:46.670
What is all this?

41:48.756 --> 41:50.007
It's quite detailed.

41:51.425 --> 41:53.219
Do you think this might be it?

41:55.012 --> 41:56.722
A fragment of our memories?

42:02.436 --> 42:06.649
All right. The two of us have lost
some memories from our past lives.

42:06.732 --> 42:08.734
Who wants to help us find them?

42:08.817 --> 42:10.861
I don't have any memories.

42:10.945 --> 42:12.655
I don't have my master's permission.

42:13.155 --> 42:15.241
-I have no intention of helping.
-[scoffs]

42:16.742 --> 42:20.579
Fine. Do you or do you not know
that Ejllael is hiding something?

42:20.663 --> 42:23.624
-I don't have any memories.
-I have no intention of helping.

42:28.504 --> 42:29.380
Irem.

42:31.423 --> 42:32.550
Just a moment.

42:36.971 --> 42:38.305
-[slashes]
-[gasps]

42:39.181 --> 42:40.599
Irem!

42:44.019 --> 42:45.396
You're one tough cookie.

42:45.980 --> 42:49.400
Have you ever seen
the two of us together in the past?

42:49.483 --> 42:51.485
Blink once if you have.

42:52.528 --> 42:53.529
Just a moment.

42:54.572 --> 42:58.075
[Sade wails] Master, isn't this too much?

42:58.158 --> 43:01.245
Must you do this to my love
for the sake of yours?

43:02.246 --> 43:04.498
Irem! [sobbing]

43:05.291 --> 43:08.252
Hey, open up.
We need to put this back, Irem.

43:08.335 --> 43:09.336
Here's an easy one.

43:10.254 --> 43:13.924
Did Genie and Jinniya kiss,
or did they not?

43:14.008 --> 43:16.010
Did he or did he not have a mouth?

43:16.510 --> 43:18.846
-I can answer that--
-Irem's out due to injuries.

43:19.430 --> 43:21.807
You and me, one on one,
with him on the line.

43:24.435 --> 43:25.936
I have plans.

43:27.646 --> 43:29.273
-[crashing]
-Oh.

43:29.940 --> 43:33.277
[Ka-young] Hmm.
So you tend to use plans as an excuse.

43:33.902 --> 43:34.737
Master!

43:35.904 --> 43:39.033
-[hoots]
-Irem, watch out for your wings!

43:39.116 --> 43:41.410
You're a national treasure!

43:41.910 --> 43:45.664
Irem! Irem!

43:48.792 --> 43:52.838
I guess we've learned one thing.
"We have a hidden past."

43:54.214 --> 43:57.551
"You kissed her." We've learned that too.

43:59.970 --> 44:01.305
I don't think that's true.

44:02.181 --> 44:03.932
[chimes]

44:05.643 --> 44:07.936
[gasps] It's Eom Sang-tae.

44:11.231 --> 44:13.442
Will he really go to the past?

44:13.525 --> 44:17.112
Even if he does,
past you wouldn't know the situation.

44:17.946 --> 44:19.448
Would you even get involved?

44:20.699 --> 44:21.700
100%.

44:23.619 --> 44:27.373
Mm. I'll probably bring the baseball bat
that's beside my wardrobe.

44:27.456 --> 44:28.749
I know myself.

44:29.249 --> 44:31.168
I'll definitely try to save that girl.

44:31.752 --> 44:33.545
-But this wish is just so…
-I know.

44:33.629 --> 44:35.297
Once again, I'll lose.

44:35.798 --> 44:38.509
And if I lose,
dying is part of my first wish.

44:39.677 --> 44:42.221
But I'll still do it.
I will make good decisions.

44:42.304 --> 44:44.723
I may have been born bad,
but I can still do that.

44:46.684 --> 44:47.726
If we're going to

44:49.019 --> 44:50.813
die anyway, might as well make it fun.

44:52.481 --> 44:54.274
So go and protect me.

44:55.067 --> 44:56.860
If I am to die, make sure it's for you.

44:57.694 --> 45:00.948
And if you are to die,
you should die for me too.

45:05.285 --> 45:06.203
All right.

45:07.162 --> 45:08.163
I'll do that.

45:10.165 --> 45:11.166
Let's do that.

45:18.132 --> 45:19.967
To right before you killed that girl?

45:20.050 --> 45:21.176
Isn't it obvious?

45:21.260 --> 45:24.138
It's a chance to feel that rush again.
Why would I waste it?

45:25.180 --> 45:28.934
This time, I won't smash her
into my taillight or dye her hair.

45:29.518 --> 45:33.480
Then they won't be able to link it
to the case from 20 years ago. [chuckles]

45:35.732 --> 45:37.025
But this time,

45:38.360 --> 45:40.737
I'm thinking of chopping her into parts.

45:41.321 --> 45:44.116
So, that's your plan?

45:45.534 --> 45:47.828
If that's how it is,
maybe I should shift gears.

45:47.911 --> 45:48.871
Do it.

45:48.954 --> 45:50.372
Do whatever it takes.

45:50.456 --> 45:52.207
You're my genie, after all.

45:52.708 --> 45:56.086
April 10, nighttime.

45:56.170 --> 45:58.881
At 9:10. That's p.m., okay?

45:59.673 --> 46:01.508
In front of the Gangma Falls sign. Got it?

46:01.592 --> 46:02.509
GANGMA FALLS, 500M

46:04.553 --> 46:05.888
100%.

46:07.097 --> 46:08.474
It's been fulfilled.

46:10.601 --> 46:12.519
[Pan-geum] What was your CSAT score?

46:12.603 --> 46:14.146
APRIL 10, 2024
20:39

46:15.939 --> 46:20.777
-[sighs] Your grandma is fuming.
-Why?

46:20.861 --> 46:21.987
Something about you

46:23.405 --> 46:24.990
doing two things at the same time.

46:25.073 --> 46:26.283
Don't ever do that again.

46:28.535 --> 46:30.370
Also, I'm here from the future.

46:31.205 --> 46:33.332
You're here from the Middle East.
Get lost.

46:34.082 --> 46:35.501
It's true.

46:36.001 --> 46:38.962
And this is a favor
your future self asked of you.

46:40.589 --> 46:41.882
Hmm?

46:47.054 --> 46:49.598
WRITTEN BY KI KA-YOUNG
A NEGATIVE ONE AND A STONE…

46:52.267 --> 46:53.101
[chuckles]

46:59.358 --> 47:01.443
EOM SANG-TAE IS THE MURDERER
HE WILL KILL AGAIN

47:01.527 --> 47:04.446
20-YEAR-OLD CORPSE FOUND
IN CHEONGPUNG VILLAGE

47:04.530 --> 47:08.075
[tense music playing]

47:08.158 --> 47:11.328
HIS SIGNATURE SEEMS TO BE
DYEING HIS VICTIMS' HAIR BLACK

47:11.411 --> 47:14.581
SHE WILL GO MISSING TONIGHT
(APRIL 10, 2024) AROUND 9 P.M.

47:18.043 --> 47:20.128
I knew this bastard would do this.

47:24.299 --> 47:25.259
You were right.

47:26.260 --> 47:27.594
You'd be late going that way.

47:31.056 --> 47:32.224
Hold on tight.

47:36.478 --> 47:38.480
[tense music continues playing]

47:39.815 --> 47:41.984
[chuckling]

47:44.027 --> 47:46.947
[soft chiming]

47:52.202 --> 47:54.246
Mm. Mm?

47:58.417 --> 48:00.252
I could swear I've been here before.

48:05.299 --> 48:06.883
Right, April.

48:08.218 --> 48:09.553
[woman] Mr. Eom.

48:13.098 --> 48:15.434
What the hell?

48:16.476 --> 48:17.477
I definitely remember…

48:18.145 --> 48:19.855
I'm so sorry.

48:19.938 --> 48:23.525
I just realized I left my phone behind
at the bus terminal.

48:23.609 --> 48:24.610
Your phone?

48:32.784 --> 48:34.828
I must've just imagined it.

48:34.911 --> 48:37.372
-[chuckling]
-[ominous music playing]

48:37.456 --> 48:39.708
Yes, that's right. Your cell phone.

48:39.791 --> 48:41.793
-Please come this way.
-Thanks.

48:43.795 --> 48:44.838
I must say…

48:47.633 --> 48:50.719
the more I look at it,
the blonder it seems.

48:50.802 --> 48:53.138
-Your hair, I mean.
-[chuckles nervously]

48:53.221 --> 48:54.056
Sorry?

48:57.976 --> 48:59.895
-[grunting]
-[woman whimpering]

49:02.731 --> 49:05.192
-[whimpering]
-[giggling]

49:07.194 --> 49:08.820
-Where are you going?
-[screams]

49:08.904 --> 49:10.697
Come here, you fucking bitch!

49:11.573 --> 49:14.451
-[grunts and groans]
-[woman whimpering]

49:17.829 --> 49:18.747
[Sang-tae] Fuck.

49:18.830 --> 49:20.666
Man, I should reflect on my actions.

49:20.749 --> 49:25.045
He even bought a chainsaw, but I left
his body behind and just brought his soul.

49:26.171 --> 49:28.131
Ms. Ki.

49:29.424 --> 49:30.634
Why are you doing this?

49:31.385 --> 49:34.012
-There must be a misunderstanding.
-Misunderstanding?

49:34.888 --> 49:36.348
-[grunts]
-Oh!

49:36.431 --> 49:38.517
Shut up, you fucking murderer.

49:39.893 --> 49:41.019
Is this blood?

49:41.978 --> 49:44.231
You damn bitch. Why are you doing this?

49:44.314 --> 49:45.148
Why, that little…

49:45.232 --> 49:47.484
Get over here. I'll kill you too.

49:47.567 --> 49:50.112
Just cut the crap. You can't beat me.

49:51.071 --> 49:53.448
I'm having too much fun right now.

49:53.532 --> 49:55.450
-[upbeat pop music playing]
-[San-tae yelping]

49:55.534 --> 49:57.411
Gosh, that's gotta hurt.

49:58.245 --> 50:00.247
Ouch, his elbows! Damn!

50:00.330 --> 50:04.501
Sir, could you please call the police?
What should we do?

50:04.584 --> 50:08.755
I've already called the police.
112 and I go way back, you see. Ow!

50:09.965 --> 50:11.299
[yelping]

50:14.386 --> 50:15.637
That's it!

50:17.222 --> 50:20.058
[chuckling]

50:24.479 --> 50:25.981
Just now, that evil man

50:26.523 --> 50:28.108
tried to kill this lady here.

50:28.191 --> 50:30.485
He smashed her head
against the tail light here.

50:30.986 --> 50:35.574
You can see her hair here.
And this woman here hit that man…

50:36.742 --> 50:37.909
Let's skip that part.

50:38.660 --> 50:42.622
And I have a feeling that some YouTubers
will soon uncover a 20-year-old corpse.

50:42.706 --> 50:45.250
I suggest you search that man's house.

50:45.333 --> 50:47.711
Especially the basement. Hmm?

50:47.794 --> 50:49.087
How do you know…

50:50.172 --> 50:53.216
Who are you?
Were you the witness back then?

50:54.342 --> 50:57.763
It wasn't me, but I think
it might have been your mother.

50:58.263 --> 51:00.682
I also recommend you look into her.

51:00.766 --> 51:01.892
Okay, sure.

51:03.059 --> 51:03.894
Pardon?

51:08.940 --> 51:09.858
[Iblis] Oh.

51:11.109 --> 51:12.986
Was 112 always such a friendly place?

51:13.570 --> 51:15.071
They even offered me coffee.

51:15.822 --> 51:17.407
You causing trouble in the future?

51:17.991 --> 51:18.825
Here.

51:19.659 --> 51:22.871
[sighs] I can't believe
that jerk and I are of the same kind.

51:23.580 --> 51:24.414
No.

51:25.081 --> 51:26.541
He's different from you.

51:26.625 --> 51:27.959
That punk is just a murderer.

51:29.503 --> 51:31.922
You're taking my side? Hold up.

51:32.672 --> 51:34.633
Have we grown very close in the future?

51:35.175 --> 51:36.635
So I guess you've kept me alive.

51:36.718 --> 51:38.178
-[door opens]
-[woman] Excuse me.

51:40.931 --> 51:43.308
Thank you for saving me.

51:43.809 --> 51:47.229
I would have died if it weren't for you.

51:48.146 --> 51:49.773
But I'm a psychopath, you know.

51:49.856 --> 51:50.857
Sorry?

51:51.900 --> 51:54.486
Right. Ah.

51:54.569 --> 51:57.364
Then you're the psychopath
who came to save my life.

51:57.948 --> 51:59.908
I'll be thankful for the rest of my life.

52:01.034 --> 52:03.787
Well, I should get back to the station.

52:04.287 --> 52:07.999
Thank you. Thank you so much!

52:08.625 --> 52:11.920
-[footsteps receding]
-[door opens]

52:12.003 --> 52:14.673
-Hey, I've never heard that before.
-[door closes]

52:15.173 --> 52:16.216
Someone thanking me.

52:18.468 --> 52:21.096
Wow, here and in the future too.

52:21.179 --> 52:23.598
All sorts of strange things happen
when I'm with you.

52:24.808 --> 52:26.309
You are an odd little star.

52:27.602 --> 52:28.436
Star?

52:28.520 --> 52:31.356
Yes. You're
the strangest oddball of a star…

52:32.065 --> 52:33.066
Hold up.

52:34.484 --> 52:35.944
Hey. [chuckles]

52:36.862 --> 52:38.780
No. That's not what I meant.

52:38.864 --> 52:39.698
One moment.

52:43.535 --> 52:45.120
[line connects, rings]

52:45.203 --> 52:48.039
Hey, Min-ji. It's me. This girl almost got
her head bashed in,

52:48.123 --> 52:50.876
but now this guy is
suddenly talking about stars.

52:51.918 --> 52:53.628
That's right. He's not human.

52:54.212 --> 52:55.380
He's actually not human.

52:57.299 --> 52:58.133
No.

52:58.758 --> 53:00.719
-Yeah, you're right.
-[chuckles softly]

53:00.802 --> 53:02.846
Right, this is
what you were like. [laughs]

53:02.929 --> 53:05.724
[Ka-young] Wait,
I'm not saying you're wrong…

53:06.933 --> 53:07.976
Ki Ka-young.

53:09.019 --> 53:11.938
I should get back to where you are.

53:12.022 --> 53:13.982
[Ka-young] No, I'm not taking his side.

53:14.649 --> 53:16.192
Seeing you like this,

53:17.235 --> 53:19.029
I really miss you.

53:19.112 --> 53:20.447
[whooshes]

53:25.368 --> 53:26.912
[gasps] Uh--

53:27.996 --> 53:28.997
No.

53:30.206 --> 53:31.458
It wasn't even raining.

53:31.958 --> 53:33.001
Damn it.

53:34.753 --> 53:35.629
[clears throat]

53:44.137 --> 53:46.681
You're sleeping after branding
an innocent genie a perv?

53:47.265 --> 53:48.558
[groans softly]

53:51.186 --> 53:52.103
[chuckles]

53:56.358 --> 53:58.318
[soft whooshing]

54:06.242 --> 54:07.452
[sighs]

54:07.535 --> 54:08.578
[soft whooshing]

54:10.205 --> 54:12.123
And you still fall for things like this?

54:13.249 --> 54:15.710
Right, well, mm,

54:15.794 --> 54:18.463
the past version of me, you know…

54:19.506 --> 54:22.425
[romantic ballad playing]

54:32.394 --> 54:33.561
I promise.

54:34.521 --> 54:36.439
[Zahara in Arabic] That flower was
in full bloom

54:36.523 --> 54:38.316
in the wasteland of your memory.

54:38.900 --> 54:40.276
I will find my memories.

54:42.529 --> 54:43.363
Of what?

54:44.990 --> 54:45.907
You.

54:47.117 --> 54:48.243
In my lamp…

54:50.036 --> 54:52.038
out of all the words you traced over,

54:53.039 --> 54:54.624
the most common word…

55:04.801 --> 55:07.012
is habibti.

55:08.596 --> 55:10.890
What does that mean?

55:14.811 --> 55:15.854
My love.

55:18.940 --> 55:21.359
[ballad continues playing]

57:20.228 --> 57:22.230
[upbeat pop music playing]
